  <!-- 02 Made by musicians -->
  <section class="section" id="why" aria-labelledby="why-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-mark"><span class="numeral">02</span><p class="eyebrow">Made by musicians, for musicians</p></div>
      <div class="grid lp-idea">
        <div class="col-6"><h2 id="why-title">Stop Re-entering Music <span class="key">Note by Note</span>.</h2></div>
        <div class="col-6 lp-idea__body">
          <p class="lead">CuTTI Score is built by SVLS LABS for composers, arrangers, teachers and performers who work with printed music every day: the score from a library, the part from a colleague, the old edition that exists only on paper.</p>
          <p class="lp-pull">Instead of re-entering it note by note, open it in CuTTI Score, check it side by side with the original, correct what needs correcting, and carry on in the notation program you already use.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 03 What it does -->
  <section class="section band-dark" id="what-it-does" aria-labelledby="does-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
        <div class="section-mark"><span class="numeral">03</span><p class="eyebrow">What it does</p></div>
        <h2 id="does-title">Everything Between the Printed Page and Your Notation Program.</h2>
      </div>
      <ul class="lp-get" role="list">
        <li><h3 class="h4">Reads printed music</h3><p>PDFs from notation programs, scanned editions, phone photos taken at the stand, and screenshots. Single pages or whole scores of hundreds of pages.</p></li>
        <li><h3 class="h4">Keeps the look of the print</h3><p>Instrument names and abbreviations, braced piano staves, systems and pages as printed, titles and credits, lyrics, dynamics, articulations, beams, ties and slurs.</p></li>
        <li><h3 class="h4">Lets you check and correct</h3><p>The original and the reading side by side, with a confidence map that takes you straight to the bars to check. Editing tools to add, delete, split or merge bars, fix a clef or key, move notes between voices, copy and paste, type lyrics, and add dynamics, tempo marks and text, all with full undo.</p></li>
        <li><h3 class="h4">Plays it back</h3><p>Real instrument sounds, a mixer with volume, pan, mute and solo for each part, and transposition to any key.</p></li>
        <li><h3 class="h4">Hands it on</h3><p>Open in Dorico, Sibelius, Finale or MuseScore in one step; export MusicXML, MIDI, PDF and audio; one file per part for the players; print.</p></li>
        <li><h3 class="h4">Works with sound too</h3><p>Turn a recording into a score as a starting point.</p></li>
        <li><h3 class="h4">Private by design</h3><p>Recognition runs entirely on your Mac. Nothing you scan or record is uploaded.</p></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 04 How it works -->
  <section class="section" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="how-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head" data-reveal>
        <div class="section-mark"><span class="numeral">04</span><p class="eyebrow">How it works</p></div>
